  "script": "In 1850, a lighthouse stood on the rocks above the harbour. Every evening at dusk, the keeper climbed one hundred and twelve steps to light the lamp. The old harbour map shows why the light mattered. Three reefs lay hidden just outside the harbour mouth. A ship coming in at night had to pass between them. The great lens gathered the small flame into one strong beam. On a clear night, sailors could see it twenty miles away. In winter storms the keeper stayed awake until morning. Thanks to the light, the ships came home safely.",
